{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Design review decisions (operator-approved 2026-08-02):\n\n1. Change 1 is REVISED from 'hourly cadence' to the pattern zero-downtime OSS deployments converge on: QUIESCE, don't rarefy.\n   a. Deploy only when the image/main actually changed — the autodeploy service must no-op when there is nothing new to deploy (this also addresses the unexplained ch1193 collision, where no main commit landed in the review window: a redeploy with no new commit should never have restarted the container).\n   b. A 20-minute drain is APPROVED: size stop_grace_period (and the container's shutdown drain) to cover the measured max review duration (~911s observed; 20min gives headroom) rather than only the 150s store-write tail. This is the Kubernetes terminationGracePeriodSeconds/preStop pattern — the deploy waits for in-flight work instead of killing it. The 2-minute timer cadence can then stay (a deploy that quiesces is safe at any cadence), though hourly remains acceptable as belt-and-braces.\n\n2. Change 2 (fail-NO-VOTE for retryable) confirmed as specified — it matches how Zuul (jobs interrupted by executor restart are retried without reporting) and Prow (evicted jobs rescheduled) behave; the bounded-retry escalation mirrors Zuul's RETRY_LIMIT. On the open 'indeterminate' judgement call: by those systems' semantics, a review that RAN TO COMPLETION and concluded 'cannot determine' is a result -> VOTE -1 (terminal); only teardown/infra paths are vote-less.\n\n3. Harmonize with bb9b: the bounded-retry state (attempt counter per revision) must be a shared mechanism — bb9b's contributor trigger acts as 'reset the retry budget and re-drive' on the same state, not a parallel retry system. Land this ticket first; design the retry-bound storage so bb9b can reuse it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785695719084075001,"uuid":"3ba352a7-5ca6-4e12-86e7-d1f04c2cdd15"}